== A State initializer is skipped as a unit: the field names of a named
== construction (`X := 1, Y := 2`) are not State declarations (CANON-9). With
== the old token scanner, `Y` became a phantom State symbol and the explicit
== local declaration of `Y` below failed as shadowing.
Module StateNamedConstructionInitializer

Type
    TPoint Struct
        X Integer
        Y Integer
    ;

State :
    Origin TPoint := TPoint(X := 1, Y := 2)
    Count Integer := 0
;

Main :
    Y Integer := 3
    PutLn(Y)
;
